    <string name="rcp_ingredients">Ingredients:</string>
    <string name="rcp_tools">Tools:</string>
    <string name="rcp_steps">Steps</string>
    <string name="rcp_steps_of">Steps to make %1$s</string>
    <string name="rcp_ubee_step_1">Mix the flour, salt, milk and melted butter. Knead until smooth and elastic.</string>
    <string name="rcp_ubee_step_2">Let the dough rest for 1 hour, covered with plastic wrap.</string>
    <string name="rcp_ubee_step_3">Mix the mashed purple sweet potato with sweetened condensed milk.</string>
    <string name="rcp_ubee_step_4">Roll out the dough, add mozzarella, purple sweet potato, then more mozzarella. Shape and seal.</string>
    <string name="rcp_ubee_step_5">Cook in a non-stick pan over low heat, brushing with butter.</string>
    <string name="rcp_ubee_step_6">Cook 5–8 minutes per side until golden brown and the cheese melts. Remove and serve.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_step_1">Steam the sweet potato until soft, then mash. Set some aside for the filling.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_step_2">Mix the tapioca flour, wheat flour, sugar and salt.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_step_3">Add melted butter, egg and milk. Stir into a soft dough that can be shaped.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_step_4">Mix the mashed sweet potato with sweetened condensed milk into a smooth filling.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_step_5">Divide the dough into 6 portions and flatten each one.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_step_6">Put the filling in the middle, then close and shape it like a sweet potato. Place on a tray lined with baking paper. Bake at 170°C for ±20–25 minutes until cooked.</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_note_1">Ready to enjoy!</string>
    <string name="rcp_goguma_note_2">Remove and serve warm</string>
    <string name="rcp_taro_step_1">Steam the taro until soft, then mash until smooth with no lumps.</string>
    <string name="rcp_taro_step_2">Mix the taro with butter, milk powder, egg yolk, salt, pepper and nutmeg. Stir until the dough can be shaped.</string>
    <string name="rcp_taro_step_3">Take 1 tbsp of dough and flatten it, then put a piece of mozzarella in the middle. Seal tightly and shape into a ball or oval.</string>
    <string name="rcp_taro_step_4">Coat in flour → egg → breadcrumbs until the whole surface is covered.</string>
    <string name="rcp_taro_step_5">Chill in the fridge for 15–30 minutes so the coating holds better. Then fry until golden brown.</string>
